Gungnir:

It's built on Singularity Framework
It's a spear weapon (pierce) that can also be thrown
It should be better than persona monosword
Gungnir NEVER misses
Unworthy pawns are not rejected (rejectsUnworthy = false). They can hold it, throw it and recall it.
Partial aptitude lowers Gungnir's own stats through the framework's stat factors.
On recall, Gungnir comes back and has to be caught: if youre unworthy you get slammed with the full force of the weapon and have to
take time to rip it out. Ripping it out causes damage. Works anywhere on the map and gungnir just comes back
It goes around mountains and walls and slams through every door on the way, even locked ones. It damages anyone standing between it and the wielder; Damages anything it pierces
Throwing leaves the wielder without Gungnir

If anything happens to the impaled body (it dies, is destroyed, leaves the map or gets carried off), Gungnir flies back on its own.
If the wielder isn't on the map, it drops where the body was last seen.
If the wielder is gone (dead, downed or off the map) while Gungnir is lodged, it stays lodged until it's ripped out by anyone.

Gungnir hitting a target stuns the target

Gungnir's droning:
Those impaled by the harpoon are pulverized as successive strikes amplify its vibrating force.
Attacking a target with gungnir increases droning: amplifies damage taken
Does not decay
Every attack gives 1% to severity
Gungnir returning uses up all droning for a big damage payoff after leaving the target
Gungnir's droning only works with "alive" targets (not a corpse)


